Hi Rahul,

As discussed during our recent conversation regarding your career growth
and current role expectations, we also discussed certain areas where
further improvement in skill development, and capability enhancement would
be required to support your continued growth within the organization. We
understand that, considering these aspects, you have been evaluating
opportunities outside the organization, along with your personal business
plans.

During the discussion, you also expressed your willingness to move on from
the organization and requested an early relieving, considering the offers
you currently have in hand. We appreciate the openness and transparency
with which you shared your thoughts and future plans with us.

Accordingly, rather than moving forward with discussions around your
current role expectations and performance-related processes, we would like
to understand your preferred timeline for transition and relieving. This
will help us plan the necessary work handover and ensure a smooth
transition for both you and the organization.

Please let us know your expected last working date or the earliest date by
which you would like to be relieved.

We will review your requested date based on business requirements, project
commitments, and the required handover, and we will try our best to
facilitate the transition at the earliest possible date.

We value your contribution and want to ensure a professional and respectful
transition.

For any further clarification regarding the terms and conditions of your
employment, please refer to your appointment letter.



Regards,
Sr. HR Manager

Konstant Infosolutions Pvt Ltd

